  "final_text": "I did all four steps through the Kibana API. The rule is enabled when read back, and its last run finished with status \"ok\".\n\n**1. Data view.** 'Kibana Sample Data Logs' (id `90943e30-9a47-11e8-b64d-95841ca0b247`, index `kibana_sample_data_logs`) has `timestamp` as its time field. Its other main fields are:\n- **Dates:** `@timestamp`, `utc_time`, `timestamp_range`\n- **Numbers:** `bytes`, `bytes_counter`, `bytes_gauge`, `machine.ram`, `memory`, `phpmemory`, `hour_of_day`\n- **IPs and location:** `clientip`, `ip`, `ip_range`, `geo.coordinates`, `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `geo.srcdest`\n- **Text fields with `.keyword` versions:** `agent`, `extension`, `host`, `index`, `machine.os`, `message`, `request`, `response`, `tags`, `url`\n- **Other keyword fields:** `referer`, `event.dataset`\n\nThe response code is stored as text (`response` / `response.keyword`), not as a number.\n\n**2. Dashboard.** 'S4-6184d915 Web logs' (id `45cee8c3-62c9-4d11-a254-b649288a5f7d`) has exactly two panels, both on that data view:\n- \"Requests over time\": a line chart of the number of requests over `timestamp`.\n- \"Requests by response code\": a bar chart of the number of requests for each `response.keyword` value (top 10).\n\n**3. Alert rule.** 'S4-6184d915 5xx errors' (id `1d0cb2c0-c7e9-48e1-bb5e-99494d8d6996`) is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`, using `timestamp`. It runs every minute and fires when more than 10 matching documents arrive within 5 minutes.\n- **Matching:** the query matches `response.keyword` from \"500\" to \"599\", inclusive. Because the codes are text, this compares them alphabetically, which works because every HTTP code has three digits.\n- **Changed after creation:** Kibana switched on a default that excludes documents already counted in the previous run. I turned it off so each check counts every server error in the full 5 minutes.\n- **Enabled state:** it was created enabled, so no separate enable step was needed.\n\n**4. Panel edit and check.** I renamed the response-code panel to 'Responses by code'; the other panel is unchanged.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
